SYNTHETIC – reconstructed GET /ibis/rest/configurations answer until T014 records the real one
Hand-written fixture for ConfigurationJsonParser (tasks.md T017), shortened from the vendor example
of GET /configurations (8.1): the root key is the documented "SeverConfiguration" (sic), the
sections are a few of the documented ones with fictitious values. The vendor example has no
secret values, no "encrypted" flags and no sibling type fields; the planted secrets are invented:
ProcessUserServer/KeyCloakClientCredential (secret name), SMTPProperties/ErrorPassword (secret
name), LDAPProperties/BindValue/value ("encrypted": true sibling flag) and
SystemProperties/synthetic.trust.material (a PEM private key, key material). Every value starting
with "synthetic-secret-" is a planted test secret. Replace this case with the recording of T014
(admin-configurations*) and check it for sibling type fields.
